# API (Vercel Serverless)

- All routes and helpers needed at runtime live **inline** in `api/index.ts`; `vercel.json` routes `/api/*` to it
- Shared types: `import type { ... } from "../shared/api"` only. Runtime imports from `../shared/` break Vercel (`npm run check:api-inline`)
- Wrap every handler in `route(...)`; throw `new HttpError(status, "errors.key", data?)`; responses are `{ ok: true, ... }` or `{ error: "<i18n key>" }`
- Validate bodies with `zod`; never trust ids/tenant from the body — tenant comes from `requireTenant(perm)` (`X-Tenant-Id` header or session) and every query filters `tenant_id = ?`
- Guards: `requireAuth()`, `requireTenant(TenantPerm)`, `requirePlatform(PlatformPerm)`
- Grid endpoints: `parseGridQuery(req.query, SPEC, baseWhere, baseParams)` + `runGrid(...)` → `{ items, pagination }`. Sort keys and filter values are **whitelists** in the spec
- Use `db.query` / `db.exec` / `db.tx` (never the pool directly) so the unit project can swap in `api/testFakeDb.ts`
- Audit sensitive writes with `audit(req, action, entity, id, { tenantId, actorId, meta })`
- **ALWAYS update `api/swagger.yaml`** in the same change when endpoints, payloads, responses, or behavior change
- Email only through `sendEmail(...)` (logs to `email_log`, dry-run in tests / without `RESEND_API_KEY`)
- Vitest: never send live Resend mail; integration fixtures use `fixturePrefix(suite)` emails and `cleanupByPrefix` in `afterAll`
